      "note": "2025 London orthophoto. Roof patch at local [125.22, 55.62] averages #c3c9bb."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "frame": "103297209",
      "walls": [
        0
      ],
      "note": "White elevated enclosed link with continuous dark triangular glazed intervals. Brick and stone buildings occupy much of the view and attribution of the low south face is uncertain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "frame": "131413433",
      "walls": [
        0
      ],
      "note": "Link spans the open drive with daylight underneath. Its roofline is lower than the medical sciences mass behind it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Rectangular south roof, narrow crosswise link and a plant-filled northern roof with bright sheet metal, an L-shaped fan array and ducts."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://norlon.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/WesternBioMed-web-1-1.jpg",
      "walls": [
        0,
        3
      ],
      "note": "Completion photograph. The single exposed storey has high rectangular stone-framed lights, projecting masonry piers with pale stepped caps and a raised landing in front of a grey door."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/univsec/pdf/board/minutes/2023/a23June29bg_PGN_website.pdf#page=26",
      "walls": [
        0
      ],
      "note": "June 2023 capital project photograph identifies the south facade. The long rough-faced stone wall rises behind stairs and a glass guard."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/fm/img/projects/880x300_biomed.jpg",
      "note": "Facilities elevation shows stone-clad terraces stepping down the slope toward dark-framed glazing. The existing skywalk meets the upper end."
    },
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/fm/projects/capital_projects/biomedical_research.html",
      "note": "Western records construction beginning after 2019 excavation and three levels, two below the Elgin Road side."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "2017 ground survey puts the bridge drive about 5.5 m above the inventory datum. A 10.75 m soffit therefore clears the drive by approximately 5.25 m."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.balanengineering.com/projects/western-bridge",
      "note": "The 2024 construction photographs show a white rectangular trussed span beside the finished stone frontage. Continuous blue glass and white diagonal members are visible in the exterior view of the east link."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Narrow enclosed roof crosses the open yard on a separate north–south line east of the plant. Its southern landing and the short western connection are visible in the orthophoto. Elevations of these links are approximate."
    }
  ],
